.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PLAKAR-IMMICH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm plakar-immich
.Nd Plakar plugin to back up and restore an Immich user or server
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
plugin speaks two protocols.
.Pp
.Li immich://
backs up one Immich user through the Immich API and restores the
result into an Immich user, on the same server or another one.
It needs an API key and nothing else, so it works against hosted
instances.
The backup holds the originals as plain files with their XMP sidecars,
and the user's albums, stacks, tags, named people and face boxes as
small JSON files keyed by the assets' SHA1 checksums.
A restore uploads what the target does not have yet, then recreates the
relations; assets already on the target are skipped, albums and people
of the same name are reused.
.Pp
.Li immich+dump://
backs up a whole server the way Immich recommends: a fresh database
dump taken through the admin API, then the files of its
.Ev UPLOAD_LOCATION
when it is reachable from the host running plakar.
A restore replaces the target's database through the server's own
maintenance restore, writes the files back and regenerates the
thumbnails; every user, API key, album, person and asset id comes back.
See
.Sx IMMICH+DUMP
below.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The parameters of
.Li immich://
are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar location
.Li immich://host[:port][/prefix] .
HTTPS is used unless the host is loopback.
.It Ar api_key
The Immich API key of the user.
.Ev PLAKAR_IMMICH_API_KEY
in the environment takes precedence and keeps the key off the command
line.
.It Ar insecure
.Li true
to skip the verification of the server's TLS certificate.
.It Ar plaintext
.Li true
to talk HTTP instead of HTTPS.
.El
.Sh LAYOUT
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/manifest.json
/assets/2024/07/IMG_0123.HEIC        original
/assets/2024/07/IMG_0123.HEIC.xmp    sidecar when present
/assets/2024/07/IMG_0123.HEIC.json   metadata, tags, people
/albums/<name>.json
/stacks/<primary sha1>.json
/people/<name>.json
.Ed
.Pp
Assets are filed by the local date Immich shows them under; a name
collision in the same month gets the first eight hex digits of the
checksum appended.
.Sh WHAT DOES NOT COME BACK
Assets in the locked folder are invisible to API keys and are not in
the backup.
Assets shared by a partner belong to the other user.
Asset ids, creation dates, memories, shared links, the user's own API
keys and PIN, and OCR text are not restorable through the API.
Faces come back as manual boxes on the same named people; unnamed
people found by machine learning are left for the target to find
again.
.Sh IMMICH+DUMP
.Li immich+dump://host[:port][/prefix]
takes an admin API key.
The parameters are
.Ar location ,
.Ar api_key ,
.Ar insecure
and
.Ar plaintext
as above, and:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar upload_location
The server's
.Ev UPLOAD_LOCATION
as seen from this host.
When set, the backup walks it after the dump and the restore writes it
back.
.Li thumbs/
and
.Li encoded-video/
are left out, the server regenerates them.
.It Ar maintenance_token
On a restore into a server that has no admin user yet, the maintenance
token printed in the server log.
.Ev PLAKAR_IMMICH_MAINTENANCE_TOKEN
in the environment takes precedence.
.It Ar force
.Li true
to restore a dump made by another Immich or Postgres version, or one
whose name carries no version.
.It Ar dump_timeout
How long a backup waits for the server's dump job, default
.Li 15m .
.It Ar restore_timeout
How long a restore waits for the maintenance restore, default
.Li 1h .
.El
.Pp
The snapshot holds the dump as
.Pa /backups/immich-db-backup-<ts>-v<immich>-pg<postgres>.sql.gz
and the files under
.Pa /upload_location/ .
The dump comes first, so a backup taken while the server runs can at
worst hold files the database does not know about.
.Pp
A backup queues the
.Li backup-database
job and polls the list of dumps until the new one is listed, which the
server only does once the file is complete.
.Pp
A restore reads the Immich and Postgres versions from the dump's name
and refuses to go on unless they match the target, Immich exactly and
Postgres by major, the latter from the dumps the target made itself
since nothing else exposes it; a target with no dump of its own skips
that check.
It then uploads the dump, which the server stores as
.Li uploaded-<name> ,
starts the
.Li restore_database
maintenance action with that name, and polls the maintenance status
while the server dumps a restore point, restarts into its maintenance
worker, restores, migrates and restarts again; the API is away for a
couple of seconds at each restart.
The files are then written back with the fs exporter and the
.Li thumbnailGeneration
job is started.
One dump is restored per run.
.Pp
On a configured server an admin API key is all it takes.
A fresh server, with no admin yet, has to be put in its restore flow
first with
.Li POST /api/admin/database-backups/start-restore
or
.Dq Restore from backup
on its setup page; it then restarts into maintenance mode and prints
.Li https://my.immich.app/maintenance?token=<JWT>
in its log.
That token, valid four hours, is the
.Ar maintenance_token .
Calling
.Li start-restore
again voids it.
Without it the restore refuses and says so.
The API key given to such a restore must exist in the dump: it becomes
valid once the dump is in and is what starts the thumbnail job.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PLAKAR_IMMICH_MAINTENANCE_TOKEN
.It Ev PLAKAR_IMMICH_API_KEY
The API key, ahead of the
.Ar api_key
parameter.
.It Ev PLAKAR_IMMICH_MAINTENANCE_TOKEN
The maintenance token of a fresh server, ahead of the
.Ar maintenance_token
parameter.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Back up a user:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ export PLAKAR_IMMICH_API_KEY=...
$ plakar at /path/to/repo backup immich://photos.example.org
.Ed
.Pp
Restore the snapshot into a fresh server, as another user:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ export PLAKAR_IMMICH_API_KEY=...
$ plakar at /path/to/repo restore -to immich://127.0.0.1:2283 <snapid>
.Ed
.Pp
Restore the originals alone to a directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar at /path/to/repo restore -to /tmp/photos <snapid>
.Ed
.Pp
Back up a server as a dump plus its files, with an admin key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ export PLAKAR_IMMICH_API_KEY=...
$ plakar at /path/to/repo backup -o upload_location=/srv/immich/library immich+dump://127.0.0.1:2283
.Ed
.Pp
Restore it into a fresh server:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:2283/api/admin/database-backups/start-restore
$ docker logs immich_server 2>&1 | grep -o 'maintenance?token=.*'
$ export PLAKAR_IMMICH_MAINTENANCE_TOKEN=...
$ plakar at /path/to/repo restore -to immich+dump://127.0.0.1:2283 -o upload_location=/srv/immich/library <snapid>
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr plakar 1 ,
.Lk https://immich.app/docs/api
